00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:50.440
the same harness to benchmark coding style and tool-calling stability. On the research side,

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:55.540
authors built a 3.4 million concept UMLS knowledge graph in Neo4j,

00:05:56.020 --> 00:06:01.680
derived a 100 million token corpus, and compared continual pre-training against GraphRag at inference time

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:09.440
on LLAMA 3-8b. GraphRag delivers more than 3-5 point gains on PubMed QA and BioASQ without any

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:14.360
retraining while offering transparent multi-hop reasoning. Biomedical AI teams can download the

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:19.380
processed Neo4j graph today and test both injection strategies against their current rag pipelines.

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:24.940
There is also a useful community thread discussing realistic VRM and quantization requirements for

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:33.360
running the full 265,000 context, KimiK 2.6 model at 25-30 tokens per second on consumer hardware,

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:39.400
including notes on turboquant for the KV cache. It is a solid reference for anyone evaluating high

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:44.560
context local deployment trade-offs. Okay, let's pop the hood on sparse auto encoders because

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:50.580
everyone talks about them as a magical x-ray for LLM's that instantly reveals concepts. In practice,

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:55.900
they are a carefully tuned unsupervised dictionary learning pipeline whose success hinges on three

00:06:55.900 --> 00:07:02.480
intertwined engineering choices most papers gloss over. Start with the core insight. An SAE learns an

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:08.280
over-complete basis of sparse monosamantic features by reconstructing residual stream activations

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:14.500
while penalizing L1 norm on the hidden codes. The encoder is a simple linear layer plus real U.

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:19.980
The decoder tries to reconstruct the original activation with as few active features as possible.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:26.400
The magic emerges only when you scale the dictionary size to 16 to 64 times the original dimension

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:32.320
and train on billions of tokens with carefully annealed auxiliary losses that prevent feature collapse.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:38.460
The next layer of reality is the reconstruction sparsity trade-off. Larger dictionaries yield more

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:45.160
interpretable features but explode GPU memory and demand aggressive top-k or entropy-based sparsification

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:51.640
during training. Most production SAEs run with K equals 32 to 128 active features per token.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:59.200
Pushing below K equals 16 usually destroys downstream probe accuracy while K greater than 256 starts

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:05.780
reintroducing polysementicity. Training stability is notoriously brittle. Small changes in learning

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:11.540
rate or warm-up schedule can cause entire feature families to die. Latency and memory numbers are

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:19.500
equally concrete. Attaching a 16 times SAE to every layer of a 9 billion parameter model adds roughly

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:27.520
35 to 45 percent more parameters. It can increase forward past time by 12 to 18 percent on A100 class

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:33.160
hardware, unless you fuse the SAE matrix multiplies into the main transformer kernels.

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:39.460
The quality gain plateaus sharply above roughly 70 billion parameter models because larger models

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:45.380
already learn more disentangled representations in the base training run. So when should you actually

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:51.640
reach for this versus the alternative? Use SAEs when you need mechanistic explanations,

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:57.160
red teaming, or hallucination probes on mid-size models between 7 and 70 billion parameters,

00:08:57.540 --> 00:09:02.000
for pure performance, distillation, or targeted supervised probes remain cheaper.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:08.360
The gacha that bites most teams is treating SAE features as ground truth instead of noisy,

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:14.380
training data-dependent approximations. Always validate discovered hallucination features with

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:19.220
causal interventions before trusting them in production guardrails. If you are building agents

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:24.140
for financial services, try Metacomps governance framework this week. The structured audit and

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:29.160
intervention primitives let you move from sandbox to regulated production faster than custom compliance

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:35.720
layers. Run your current geometry model through the Georep Evil parallel formulation test set.

